# Okur's help keys, shown in the Virtual Viewer as JAWS shows its own: screen-sensitive help
# (Insert+F1), the hot keys (Insert+H) and the Windows keys (Insert+W). The keys and where the
# text is shown follow JAWS; the words are Okur's own (JAWS's help texts are Freedom
# Scientific's).

# Screen-sensitive help (Insert+F1): what the focused control is for, and its keys.
help-control-edit = Type here. The arrow keys move through the text and read what they pass.
help-control-text-area = Type here. Up and Down Arrow move by line, and Insert+Down reads from the cursor to the end.
help-control-check-box = Press the Spacebar to check or clear this box.
help-control-radio-button = Up and Down Arrow choose another option of this group.
help-control-combo-box = Up and Down Arrow, or an item's first letter, choose an item. Alt+Down Arrow opens the list.
help-control-list-box = Up and Down Arrow move through this list, and an item's first letter goes to it.
help-control-list-view = The arrow keys move through this list. Ctrl+Insert with a number reads that column of the item.
help-control-tree-view = Up and Down Arrow move through the tree. Right Arrow opens an item and Left Arrow closes it.
help-control-button = Press the Spacebar or Enter to use this button.
help-control-tab = Ctrl+Tab goes to the next page and Ctrl+Shift+Tab to the one before; the arrow keys also choose a tab.
help-control-slider = The arrow keys change the value, and Page Up and Page Down change it in bigger steps.
help-control-menu = Up and Down Arrow move through the menu, Enter chooses an item and Escape closes the menu.
help-control-link = Press Enter to follow this link.
help-control-cell = The arrow keys move between cells, and Ctrl+Home and Ctrl+End go to the first and the last cell.
help-control-other = Tab goes to the next control and Shift+Tab to the one before. Insert+Tab says where you are.
help-page = This is a web page, read with the virtual cursor. The arrow keys read it, H moves by heading, K by link and F by form field. Insert+F6 lists the headings and Insert+F7 the links. Enter on a form field lets you type in it.

# Hot key help (Insert+H): its first line, then one link per key, which Enter uses.
help-hot-keys-intro = Okur keys for this window. Press Enter on one to use it.
help-hot-keys-page-intro = Okur keys for this page. Press Enter on one to use it.
help-key-say-all = Read from here to the end, Insert+Down Arrow
help-key-headings-list = List the headings, Insert+F6
help-key-links-list = List the links, Insert+F7
help-key-form-fields-list = List the form fields, Insert+F5
help-key-element-lists = More lists of the page's elements, Insert+F3
help-key-find = Find text on the page, Ctrl+F
help-key-control-help = Help on the current control, Insert+F1
help-key-windows-keys = Keys Windows gives every application, Insert+W
help-key-window-title = Say the window's title, Insert+T
help-key-read-window = Read the window, Insert+B
help-key-current-control = Say the current control, Insert+Tab
help-key-default-button = Say a dialog box's default button, Insert+E
help-key-window-list = List the open windows, Insert+F10
help-key-time = Say the time, Insert+F12
help-key-settings-in-use = Say the settings in use, Insert+Q
help-key-quick-settings = Change Okur's settings, Insert+V
help-key-virtualize-window = Show the window's text in the Virtual Viewer, Insert+Alt+W

# Windows keys help (Insert+W).
help-windows-intro = Keys Windows gives every application:
help-windows-menu-bar = Alt or F10 goes to the application's menu bar.
help-windows-start = The Windows key, or Ctrl+Escape, opens the Start menu.
help-windows-switch = Alt+Tab switches to another open window.
help-windows-close = Alt+F4 closes the window in front.
help-windows-context-menu = The Applications key, or Shift+F10, opens the context menu of what has the focus.
help-windows-properties = Alt+Enter shows the properties of the selected item.
help-windows-desktop = Windows+D shows the desktop, and Windows+M minimizes every window.
help-windows-tray = Windows+B goes to the notification area.
help-windows-help = F1 opens the application's own help.
